{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Vengeance and recompense are Mine.</b> With Me is the punishment of vengeance prepared and ready, and He repays them according to their deeds — the vengeance repays them their due. And there are those who interpret <b>ושלם</b> as a noun, like וְשִׁלּוּם, and it is from the root of ״וְהַדִּבֵּר אֵין בָּהֶם״ (Jeremiah 5) — like וְהַדִּבּוּר. And when will I repay them?" "<b>When their foot slips.</b> When the merit of their fathers, upon which they lean, comes to an end." "<b>For the day of their calamity is near.</b> From the time I desire to bring their calamity upon them, it is near and ready before Me to bring through many agents." "<b>And Haste — things prepared for them.</b> And what is destined for them will come swiftly." "<b>And Haste.</b> Like ״יְמַהֵר יָחִישָׁה״ (Isaiah 5). Up to here Moses testified against them words of rebuke, so that this song would serve as testimony — when the punishment comes upon them they will know that I forewarned them from the start. From here on he testified against them words of consolation, that will come upon them when the punishment is finished, all as he said above: ״וְהָיָה כִי יָבֹאוּ עָלֶיךָ וגו׳ הַבְּרָכָה וְהַקְּלָלָה וגו׳ וְשָׁב ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֶת שְׁבוּתְךָ וגו׳״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:30.513881135Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}